The user requests an Inspect in Logfire button and supplies a public
sharing URL for The open hand's tournament. Verify the complete trace
before attaching that exact URL to its stored trace identifier.

A fresh signed-out browser opens the supplied public link. All 94
records match the expected root, three matches, thirty rounds, and sixty
decisions. Every observation and decision matches the stored replay.
Resource identifiers are redacted; no HTTP metadata or exceptions are
present. The selected root span and replay identifier match.

Other games receive ordinary project trace links with an explicit
account-and-project-access requirement. Official Logfire documentation
clarifies that public projects are public within the organization, not
to every signed-in account. Supported per-trace public sharing remains
manual. Do not use a connected-app browser handoff as a public URL.

Validation: 231 Python tests and ten JavaScript tests pass. The live
public action opens the verified read-only trace from a fresh browser.
